  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday) \nIssued at 901 PM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe TN Valley won't find a break from the heat in the Long Term. The\nlingering ridge across the Southeast will start to retrograde as a \ncut off low pushes into FL starting on Thursday. With a sfc high\nanchored across the east coast, highs will remain in the 90s through\nthe week. However, the low will pull additional moisture into the \nregion, pushing Heat Index values around 100 degrees, but at this\ntime below any advisory criteria. The low will slide westward \nacross the northern Gulf through the weekend, and this will allow for\na front in the Ozarks and OH Valley to dip southward towards the TN\nValley. Models still disagree on if the front will make it in or\nnot this weekend and the outcome will have an effect on our \ntemps, cloud cover, and our precip chances. If it moves through, \nwe could have a quick break in the heat but increased rain \nchances, but if it remains to our north, hot and humid conditions \nwill persist. Will stick with guidance that has the 90s lingering,\nheat index values still hovering around 100 degrees and low \nprecip chances (15-25% Sat, 20-30% Sunday). However, trends will \nbe monitored for future needed adjustments.",
